# DSH launcher config template for start.bat.
# Copy this file to .env and adjust to your machine.
#
# start.bat starts the service through a hidden Windows Task Scheduler task
# (named dsh-<profile>), so closing its window - or the launcher/shortcut that
# ran it - cannot stop the service. stop.bat ends that task and the service.
# Logs: logs\dsh-<profile>.out.log / .err.log.
#
# node_dir       - node install dir. Wins over PATH when it holds a node.exe,
#                  so this pins the Node major the repo requires (^22.19 / ^24+)
#                  even when PATH lists a stale Node first.
#                  WARNING: the key must be `node_dir` — `node_path`/`NODE_PATH`
#                  is rejected by app-boot in any .env file.
# launch_profile - profile to boot (default: web).
# launch_port    - optional --port value for the profile app.
# launch_args    - optional extra args, space-separated, no single quotes.
# launch_timeout - seconds start.bat waits for the ready URL (default: 300).
#
# None of these keys may start with DSH_: app-boot rejects that prefix in any
# .env file, so the launcher reads launch_* and translates them to argv.
#
# Proxy does NOT go here: the repo .env must not hold HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY/
# ALL_PROXY/NO_PROXY (app-boot refuses to start). Set them once as Windows
# user environment variables, or in $DSH_HOME/.env — DSH reads them itself.
#
# Windows example:
node_dir=C:\Program Files\nodejs
launch_profile=web
# launch_port=3081
# launch_args=
# launch_timeout=300
